      "id": 1242628,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "### Summary\nIn affected versions, the experimental tasks feature (`taskStore`) did not check which session created a task. Clients sharing one `InMemoryTaskStore` could list, read and cancel each other's tasks.\n\nExperimental tasks are deprecated. The 2026-07-28 specification replaced them with a redesigned extension. The best course of action is to stop using them.\n\n### Am I affected?\nOnly if your HTTP server passes `taskStore` to `McpServer` or `Server`. If `grep -ri taskstore --exclude-dir=node_modules .` finds nothing, you are not affected.\n\nAffected versions: `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` 1.24.0 through 1.31.0. The 2.x packages are not affected.\n\n### Fix\nUpgrade to `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` 1.32.0 or later. Each task is now tied to the session that created it, so a client that starts a new session can no longer reach its earlier tasks.\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, remove `taskStore`, or create one `InMemoryTaskStore` per session.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "MCP TypeScript SDK: Experimental tasks were not tied to the session that created them",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
        "CVE-2026-111767"
      ],
      "access": "public",
      "severity": "high",
      "module_name": "@modelcontextprotocol/sdk",
      "vulnerable_versions": ">=1.24.0 <1.32.0",
